[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3 uid="uid://bgubmapwharf01"]

; Lantern Wharf — the fourth map, a walled box yard at dusk (D-056).
;
; Like Kopje Crossing this scene has no geometry in it at all.
; `scripts/world/maps/wharf_map.gd` extends `StaticMap` and builds the yard in
; `_ready()` from its layout tables — the floor, the container walls, the boxes
; and crates, four of which are hollow and open at both ends, and the works: two
; forklifts, three dozen drums, pallets and pipe stock. It then calls `super()`,
; which sweeps all of that into world-space trimesh collision on layer 1, and
; then adds the dressing: floor paint, door bars, two cranes over the walls, four
; floodlights on the wall corners, fifteen strings of festoon lanterns with five
; lamps on them, the quay gear (nets, tarps, floats, tyre fenders, rope coils,
; fish crates, mooring bitts and perched gulls), sprayed container codes, the
; Factory Kit plant (D-084) and the port outside the wall — stacks, a coaster,
; a transit shed, five gantries, four fishing boats, a lighthouse and a lit town
; on the far shore, all of it in `StaticMap.BACKDROP_GROUP` and never collision.
;
; ## The 1.2x pass
;
; The yard was 36 m square and is 43.2 m. `HALF` went 18 -> 21.6 in the script
; and every position in it was multiplied by the same 1.2, except the handful of
; flush contacts (a crate against a box, a tower against the wall) which were
; re-derived from the steel they touch, and the spine, which is placed by its
; abutment with the bay towers. The markers below moved with them: every spawn,
; both bases and all three letters are the old number times 1.2 — the corner
; pockets 15.5 -> 18.6 and 13.5 -> 16.2, the bay pads 8.5 -> 10.2 and 16 -> 19.2,
; the bases and O and G 15.5 -> 18.6. `base_radius` did *not* scale: the capture
; ring is a rule of the mode rather than a feature of the map, and 4 m still
; fits the bay, which is 8.4 m across now rather than 6.6.
;
; So this file is what `static_map.gd` asks for:
;
;   Environment  a dusk `WorldEnvironment` (`wharf_env.tres`).
;   Sun          8 degrees up over the west-south-west wall, deep orange, and
;                the only light that casts. It was 17 degrees at 0.9 energy,
;                which lit the yard like a mid-afternoon and left the four
;                floodlights with nothing to do; at 8 degrees it grazes the
;                tops of the west stacks, throws aisle-long shadows, and the
;                floods are the key light the map's name claims they are. The
;                sky's disc follows this node (`moon_follow_light` in
;                `wharf_sky.tres`), so the sun you can see and the shadows on
;                the ground can never disagree. Serialised ROW-major, as every
;                `.tscn` stores a `Transform3D`.
;   Spawns       eight pads, four at each end — two in the corner pockets and
;                two in the bays either side of the base — alternating north and
;                south so a two-player match opens with the two players at
;                opposite ends. Each faces the middle. All eight are checked
;                against the physics the match will use by `tools/preview_map`,
;                which is what proves they are still on solid floor inside the
;                bigger walls.
;   Bases        Team 1 north, Team 2 south, each in the bay between two towers
;                against its back wall, behind the spine tower (D-051).
;   Letters      B, O, G on the middle line: B at the crossroads in the centre,
;                O and G in the pockets against the west and east walls, so
;                every card is the same distance from both bases.
;
; `tools/preview_map.gd` stands a Bog on every pad, `tools/parkour_report.gd`
; walks the jump graph, proves the tall stacks are out of reach and measures the
; longest sightline, and `tools/playthrough.gd` plans the capture layout off the
; declared bases — all four are in `tools/smoke_test.sh`.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/world/maps/wharf_map.gd" id="1_wharf_map"]
